{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status","id":1502114,"title":"What do I have to do to keep my high Consilium/Order Status?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-04T10:48:06-08:00","id":1502114,"title":"What do I have to do to keep my high Consilium/Order Status?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As per the thread title, what regular tasks are needed to keep Status 5 in each Pentacle Order or the Consilium itself?<br /> <br /> The backend for this, I was asking if its feasible to have a high status Pentacle mage that does not really focus on all (or the main) aspects of its Order. I am thinking someone treating the Orders as a job to be done, but not fully into the ethos of the order itself.<ul><li><b>Guardians of the Veil</b><br /> IMHO hard to pull it is a messianic religion, and lots of focus on the Labyrinths. Not many ideas here.</li> <li><b>Mysterium</b><br /> It is another Mystery religion, with magic as its divinity. I think there is lots of focus on publishing magical research. Adding content to the Athenea.</li> <li><b>Silver Ladder</b><br /> Cryptopolies and how to influence society seem to be the path of advancement. Being a teacher to other mages (not necessarily Silver Ladder) perhaps? Participating on the Consilium tasks?</li> <li><b>Free Council</b><br /> I think here is easier, seems you could do lots of low level tasks, that in aggregate help you keep the status: voting on all proposals, hosting meetings, casting spells for other members, contributing financially to the Order expenses, providing professional advice to other members, etc. I think here &quot;being a good chap&quot; counts for a lot.</li> <li><b>Adamantine Arrow</b><br /> I think this is even harder than the Mysterium, part of the motto is &quot;Service is Mastery&quot;, so lots of applied efforts are to be expected on defending other mages, training personnel, etc.</li> <li><b>Consilium</b><br /> Working in a titled capacity? Aiding the Consilium work beyond your titled position: donating or managing the Consilium locations (meeting places, storage rooms, holding cells if any), paying/contributing to the expenses of running the Consilium?</li> </ul><br /> I envision someone that understands that having high Status on an organization like the Orders has lots of material and magical advantages (Resources, Retainers, Safe Place, Alternate Identity, Artifacts, etc, etc).<br /> <br /> I would like corrections, suggestions, and comments on the list above please.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T12:01:44-08:00","id":1502120,"title":"","content":"I believe the Orders will only entrust higher levels of power to those that serve their interests well. Defending it, providing leadership, diplomatic aid, advancing its goals through exemplary service or in recognition of major breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> Any exception requires a unique political or supernatural situation, which comes with other types of strings attached.<br /> <br /> There is no reason to invest valuable resources in someone who is not committed to the prosperity of the Order as a whole, or one that is not dedicated to its philosophy.<br /> <br /> The examples you cited seem more akin to the aide of someone who has Order Status, rather than the person in charge. The tasks lack the type of added value that would make them stand out as strong candidates to be entrusted with more power.<br /> <br /> Imagine you are choosing an Adamant Sage, would you rather have it be the mage that drills new Talons occasionally and then clocks out to do their own research, or the strategist that coordinated a cross order crackdown on the Tremere and simultaneously busted their bunkers in one beautifully planned blitz? If <i>Service is Mastery</i>, then who provided the greater service to their fellows ? Who deserves to wield the power and responsibility of being called a Sage of the Adamant Way ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-04-2023, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:18:44-08:00","id":1502131,"title":"","content":"Order Status 5 (at least with respect to the Diamond Orders) implies to me being one of the inner circle of a global mystery religion. They would perhaps be personally acquainted with every other Status 5 in the world. They would be entrusted with the deepest secrets of the order and they would have been initiated into them by another who was already at that level and trusted them. Initiation into higher levels would require metaphysical tests of loyalty and commitment that would be difficult to fake for a mage. They would be responsible for the work of the order within an entire region.<br /> <br /> It is inconceivable to me that someone could get to that level without a commitment to the orders ideals (even if a heterodox/heretical interpretation of them). Or by being an actual mole with ultimately malign intent towards the order.<br /> <br /> The Free Council is somewhat different since that can come down to mundane politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:27:44-08:00","id":1502133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorganG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502131#post1502131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order Status 5 (at least with respect to the Diamond Orders) implies to me being one of the inner circle of a global mystery religion. They would perhaps be personally acquainted with every other Status 5 in the world. They would be entrusted with the deepest secrets of the order and they would have been initiated into them by another who was already at that level and trusted them. Initiation into higher levels would require metaphysical tests of loyalty and commitment that would be difficult to fake for a mage. They would be responsible for the work of the order within an entire region.<br /> <br /> It is inconceivable to me that someone could get to that level without a commitment to the orders ideals (even if a heterodox/heretical interpretation of them). Or by being an actual mole with ultimately malign intent towards the order.<br /> <br /> <b>The Free Council is somewhat different since that can come down to mundane politics.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, half of the Diamond Orders are explicitly a very devouted religion (Mysterium, Guardians of the Veil) and the other half are hard to separate from their ideals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hypothetically, let's say you have a city with lots of low skill Free Council members and one mage grows in magical skills beyond what you had: if everyone was multi degree Disciple at most, this girl is a third degree Adept, or perhaps the order only master.<br /> <br /> Would that justify having a high Status? Either trying to get in her good graces, she being influential by casting more advanced spells on behalf of the other members, if needed being able to Duel Arcane on a more even footing with other Order members, etc)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-04-2023, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T16:06:10-08:00","id":1502162,"title":"","content":"Also, there is an entire 6th order which you seem to be ignoring. Can you get order status 5 (Seers) without prelacy? If you can is it strict job first, heirarchies, and stabbing your boss in the back at the right time? Does prelacy and following your Exarch's mystery commands actually help a seer gain status? Or is it a distraction from the political infighting each minsitry has within their Pylons and/or between ministries...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T12:15:15-08:00","id":1502225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502162#post1502162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there is an entire 6th order which you seem to be ignoring. Can you get order status 5 (Seers) without prelacy? If you can is it strict job first, heirarchies, and stabbing your boss in the back at the right time? Does prelacy and following your Exarch's mystery commands actually help a seer gain status? Or is it a distraction from the political infighting each minsitry has within their Pylons and/or between ministries...</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Seers, they probably have the easiest explanation for any given promotion you'd want. You just simply have to be powerful enough to rip the people above you out of their seat. Prelacy makes that easier in some ways, but just as often can get in the way due to the subjection to Exarchial influence.<br /> <br /> On similar principles, a Status 5 Seer without Prelacy has two main advantages, assuming the principle of the first answer from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1501422#post1501422\">this post</a> doesn't apply, being that a) they're just bloody powerful, and b) they don't suffer from the metaphysical markers that marks them as a Seer*, and thus in the game of invisible masters against invisible masters, they are all the more invisible. Sure, they're not quite as trustworthy as Prelates, but on the other hand, trusting your fellow Seers is already a rigged game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For all other orders, it's a mixture of doing your job, building connections, and being reliable for excess and extraneous conflicts and concerns within your Caucus. Taking it to the most extreme end of things for likely Order Status 5 candidates, the sort of people who become Adamant Sages, Epopts, Curators/Hierophants, Arch/Deacons, and Syndics are likely the sort of people who already perform those sorts of responsibilities at their tier/level of influence. Run your cults, fulfill your oaths, seek and preserve the sacred, enable liberation and unity, work with others and work towards the Order's ends, and you too can be the belle of the Convocation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, it can't hurt to get specific, so.<ul><li>Adamantine Arrows<ul><li>As a general rule, the Talon/First Talon/Thunderbolt Guardian/Adamant Sage structure of the Arrow is easy to grok as the military equivalent of private/captain/colonel/general (taking liberties, yes), and so the major things are how well you fulfill the duties given to you by your superiors, what others tasks(/oaths) you take on yourself, and how actively you lead within your capacity. The sort of duties you deal with are going to relate to the defense of Consilium's, the Caucus, your Cabal, and Sleepers, and in the offense against Seers, Scelesti, Rapt, Tremere, Abyssal entities, and other such things, as well as the supportive and infrastructural roles (militaries need chefs, lawyers, promoters, etc., and while not all of the backup stuff is stuff a Mage might need to do, it's stuff that is better handled with enlightened will moving things along). You can broadly summarize how you gain Status in terms of how many oaths you take on and fulfill, and skillfully delegate/cooperate in order to achieve those.</li> <li>Banner Wardens possibly have a skewed relationship to the typical military approach, since the specific guardianship of certain cabals and their project can also entail how well those projects are moving along-the Warden may not be the leader of the cabal, but the effectiveness of the defence of the cabal is very rooted in how efficiently it goes, so a Banner Warden is likely to be judged (and hopefully praised) for how they help to keep things moving along to their conclusion, or at least in terms of getting results.</li> </ul></li> <li>Guardians of the Veil<ul><li>Cultors make up the main majority of Guardians and their actions, and that action is rooted in drawing in prospects, judging them after some proper challenging of the character of proespects, and then aiding the worthy discover Awakening while distracting the unworthy from it. That latter part is a little hard to judge on, because the Watchtower will shine for who they will, so the main metrics a Guardian is going to be judged on is how many meaningful prospects are the evaluating(they will judge a Guardian if they seem to just be drawing in nobodies who pretty likely will never Awaken), and how well are they mentoring new mages before introducing them to the larger mage society. Missing the facilitation of a very worthy person into Awakening or not successfully deflecting an egrigiously unworthy person from Awakening might be a mar against their reputation, and likewise successfully leading a very worthy person into Awakening or mentoring a concern into a worthwhile member of society might be a feather in their cap, but the main virtue of a Guardian is evidence that they are paying attention and working to sort the wheat from the chaff.</li> <li>Susceptors make up the other main majority of Guardians and their actions, and the main metric they're judged by is just how much actionable surveillance they're providing on the other Orders. Much like Cultors, missing an egregious problem child or not doing (proportionately) enough about them can be a mar, while catching and dealing with a problem child appropriately can be a feather in the cap, but the main metric is if the Guardian is proving they're paying attention to their fellows, identifying concerns, and coming up with actions to either guide them away from &quot;sin&quot; or plans to take out the determined.</li> <li>Emissaries have the unpleasant problem of being a neccesary but undesired role as the public face of the secret police. You don't end up as the person who everyone has all the complaints and death threats for usually by doing well in the Guardians in general, and a lot of Guardains in this role are either inspiring doubts in their competence or have proven themselves as such by burning their cover and Masques in Significant Ways. That said, the Guardians do need good relations with the other Orders (well, as good a relationship as one can have as the Order of the Despised), and not a single one of them will deny how neccesary a good distraction is for their covert operations, and while one of the advantages of being a covert organization is that you have a lot of ways to get the directives and reports moved around to who needs them, the Emissary is a very handy method for just that. So, an Emissary is judged on exactly that-how well they handle the other Orders in regards to their actions, how well they get messages to where they need to be, and how well they help cover everyone else. An Emissary doing a good enough job as the sleight of hand for the Caucus will usually disappear when the work to get them into a workable covert position is done. An Emissary not doing that will probably just find they aren't getting the tools to do the job anymore, and may find themselves softly dropped from the Order entirely. Emissaries who fuck up...well, they tend to get fucked up.</li> </ul></li> <li>Mysterium<ul><li>Acquisitors are generally judged on just what they're acquiring and how much they are. Bring in lots of good finds or some really valuable finds, the better off you are.</li> <li>Censors have a similar role to Susceptors, except it's centered on items, magic, and Mysteries more than people, and in the general they get kudos for how many days it's been since an egregious magical problem happens, coupled with how demonstrable their watching is, usually through actionable reports. The less problems there are, the better a Censor does.</li> <li>Savants are judged by how well they're acting as a repository of occult knowledge, and just how much they are. The more they become a walking library on particular subjects, the higher their Status.</li> </ul></li> <li>Silver Ladder<ul><li>Pretty much every thearch is judged by how successful their Cryptopolies (or, at least, their contribution and direction in a Cryptopoli) are, in terms of how much power they're bringing to the order, how ardent their members are, and of course how many people are Awakening in them. If you wanna be respected in the latter, you need to have a really good cult.</li> <li>You can blanket explain how Acolytes, Lictors, Factotums, and Clavigers gain status by basically doing their jobs well on top of their cult growth and rewards. Are the Acolytes keeping the Ladder running smoothly and well informed? Are the Lictors keeping up the regular reports and policing action? Are Factotums giving due diligence to the Lex Magica, both thoroughly representing people as needed in Consilium's and Cauceses while also keeping these processes moving at an appropriate pace? Are the Clavigers building powerful relationships with other organizations and representing the Silver's Ladder's beliefs and ideals in meaningful ways? More Status.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Free Council<ul><li>The Free Council is notable as being the only order that can't ignore the role of popularity in their Status. Sure, being popular is a subtly important matter in all the other Orders(even the Guardians), but the Free Council is just shy of having to openly admit to it. If you are an influential and charismatic person who people listen and take voting direction from, then you will inevitably get high status in their Assemblies, with it's final form of that being a Syndic.</li> <li>Otherwise, how diligent are you doing your job in accordance to the will of the people (or, at least, the will of an elected Strategos or an elevated Syndic)? If you're an Emissary, are you doing a good job handling relations? Are you getting in useful reports as a Citizen Agent? Are you being responsive as a Minuteman? Are you being responsible and secure as a Letter Carrier? Then congrats, Status.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Seers of the Throne<ul><li>To advance, rip down the person above you. To not lose status, kick the people below you.</li> <li>What are you bringing to the table? What are you taking advantage of? How well is that going? The more control you have over the world, the more you twist and exacerbate the problems of the world to lock down the human spirit and otherwise keep gods from contending with the Exarchs, the more you're rewarded. Honestly, though, that all comes back around to you ability to kick down the people below you and tear down the people above you.</li> </ul></li> </ul>As a broad thing, though, unless you're an absolute top dog in an order, you generally have to do more than your job-much like in life, Mages are more keen to support those who are going above and beyond, either in terms of helping out more of their peers on top of doing their job, or going an extra mile to advance the interests of the order on the whole while doing their job. Mages who tread water might not neccesarily lose rank, but might drift down in terms of status-maybe not a whole lot, if they're up high enough, but some.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Mystery Commands as a Condition that can be read, Exarchial Yantras being readable, the influence of Crowns and Demense on the general soul-shape of the actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-05-2023, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T16:22:00-08:00","id":1502254,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Mysterium specifically, I favor the interpretation that their advancement in the order is entirely predicated on initiations into the Mysteriorum Atlantean (or their local variant) - and as such occurs when they have sufficient experience to understand the next mystery.<br /> <br /> Their Order book does point out that the assigned jobs in the Order, especially for the middling ranks, tends to impede advancement, rather than help - because being an administrator, though necessary and requiring a lot of trust, knowledge, and people skills, ways into your opportunities to pursue ever stranger mysteries. Whereas those who become a magister (status 4) can basically delegate everything and pursue their own research without distraction - or run an athenaeum if they want.<br /> <br /> So I run it as being all about personal enlightenment. And they read your fate and declare what contribution you make will demonstrate readiness for the next level, so\u2026. Bad news for anyone trying to get ahead politically, but good news for the obsessive academics actually attracted to the order\u2026 if they can figure out how to cheat, shirk, and delegate any duty that\u2019s holding them back<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I\u2019ve been running a 1:1 game for a while with a Mysterium mage as the PC, who just got to status 5 - so I\u2019ve spend a lot of time thinking about the details of rank, and tweaking around the Atlantean Mystery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 02-05-2023, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T16:50:10-08:00","id":1502257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502225#post1502225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages who tread water might not neccesarily lose rank, but might drift down in terms of status-maybe not a whole lot, if they're up high enough, but some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting is that the Silver Ladder have this as an acknowledged part of their culture - the Silver Ladder 1e book talks about how &quot;retiree&quot; Masters who are of low Status and kept busy with trivial jobs aren't too uncommon. Being a Deacon is <i>stressful</i>, and sometimes it's a relief to just leave it all behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:09:29-08:00","id":1502262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502254#post1502254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Mysterium specifically, I favor the interpretation that their advancement in the order is entirely predicated on initiations into the Mysteriorum Atlantean (or their local variant) - and as such occurs when they have sufficient experience to understand the next mystery.<br /> <br /> Their Order book does point out that the assigned jobs in the Order, especially for the middling ranks, tends to impede advancement, rather than help - because being an administrator, though necessary and requiring a lot of trust, knowledge, and people skills, ways into your opportunities to pursue ever stranger mysteries. Whereas those who become a magister (status 4) can basically delegate everything and pursue their own research without distraction - or run an athenaeum if they want.<br /> <br /> So I run it as being all about personal enlightenment. And they read your fate and declare what contribution you make will demonstrate readiness for the next level, so\u2026. Bad news for anyone trying to get ahead politically, but good news for the obsessive academics actually attracted to the order\u2026 if they can figure out how to cheat, shirk, and delegate any duty that\u2019s holding them back<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I\u2019ve been running a 1:1 game for a while with a Mysterium mage as the PC, who just got to status 5 - so I\u2019ve spend a lot of time thinking about the details of rank, and tweaking around the Atlantean Mystery</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why I make a general point out of it not being enough to do your job. THe Mysterium makes a general point of it, but people in general are subject to taking a task done for granted over a while at the same time not according time to let people explore and build, and Mages in general are universally more valued in their mastery of the Arcana and arcane secrets. Even the Arrow and the Guardians, the two organizations who are probably the most interested in people doing their jobs and invested in rewarding it, defaultly assign more value to a master of an Arcana against a rank 5 member of their order, in the odd instances where one is not also the other.<br /> <br /> It's foolish to ignore the power and substance of political clout and acclaim, of course-but that power doesn't quite eclipse the ability to reshape the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-05-2023, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T11:55:57-08:00","id":1502317,"title":"","content":"I suspect at Status 5, you probably don't have to actively look for jobs. People are going to come to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T12:13:46-08:00","id":1502318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502317#post1502317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect at Status 5, you probably don't have to actively look for jobs. People are going to come to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>At Status 5*, you're the one making the jobs. Of course, this is because your job and goals have so many moving parts you have to.<br /> <br /> *Unless, of course, you're not at Status 5 for the conventional reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T13:17:01-08:00","id":1502319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502318#post1502318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Status 5*, you're the one making the jobs. Of course, this is because your job and goals have so many moving parts you have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is, you don't have to look for ways to make yourself useful. You're the person the Order looks to for guidance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T17:37:48-08:00","id":1502468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502319#post1502319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is, you don't have to look for ways to make yourself useful. You're the person the Order looks to for guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Status 5 is kind of self-sustaining?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T18:45:45-08:00","id":1502473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502468#post1502468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Status 5 is kind of self-sustaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same way being a Pope, or a politician is. As long as people support you, you have power, and you'll always have the knowledge and dirty laundry you've accrued while in the post regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T02:16:02-08:00","id":1502493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502468#post1502468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Status 5 is kind of self-sustaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less, I think.<br /> <br /> My impression from the books is that for the Diamond Orders, a status 5 mage is basically a kind of living saint (or at least they're treated that way). Most of them basically cut you loose at that point; aside from the Silver Ladder, I believe the magisters of the other Orders are basically all allowed to step back from day-to-day administration. They're available to provide guidance, and they're there in a crisis, but otherwise they're generally off doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> I feel that that kind of role is probably quite hard to mess up. Even if your advice is bad, or you step in to mess up a crisis, mages are going to blame themselves or each other before they blame the magister.<br /> <br /> The big exception is the Ladder, and... well... it explains pretty clearly why the other Orders do what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T14:22:57-08:00","id":1502539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502468#post1502468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Status 5 is kind of self-sustaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly? Putting asides some of the questions on how you got it that can affect the keeping of it, you still have to prove yourself reliable and active for the Order, and if you don't take care of your Status, you can and will lose it. The big difference about being at Status 5 is that, even if you don't have a ruling role in the Order, your main method of being reliable and active is getting other people to work on your projects and Obsessions, rather being someone who gets direction on what to do and when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T11:53:24-08:00","id":1502621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502262#post1502262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a reason why I make a general point out of it not being enough to do your job. THe Mysterium makes a general point of it, but people in general are subject to taking a task done for granted over a while at the same time not according time to let people explore and build, and Mages in general are universally more valued in their mastery of the Arcana and arcane secrets. Even the Arrow and the Guardians, the two organizations who are probably the most interested in people doing their jobs and invested in rewarding it, defaultly assign more value to a master of an Arcana against a rank 5 member of their order, in the odd instances where one is not also the other.<br /> <br /> It's foolish to ignore the power and substance of political clout and acclaim, of course-but that power doesn't quite eclipse the ability to reshape the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502493#post1502493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More or less, I think.<br /> <br /> My impression from the books is that for the Diamond Orders, a status 5 mage is basically a kind of living saint (or at least they're treated that way). Most of them basically cut you loose at that point; aside from the Silver Ladder, I believe the magisters of the other Orders are basically all allowed to step back from day-to-day administration. They're available to provide guidance, and they're there in a crisis, but otherwise they're generally off doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> I feel that that kind of role is probably quite hard to mess up. Even if your advice is bad, or you step in to mess up a crisis, mages are going to blame themselves or each other before they blame the magister.<br /> <br /> The big exception is the Ladder, and... well... it explains pretty clearly why the other Orders do what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Quick question: Do you automatically get rank when becoming a master? I know the\u200b\u200b Ladder can have low Status masters, but if you get too good, are you kicked upstairs?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T12:22:29-08:00","id":1502624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502621#post1502621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Quick question: Do you automatically get rank when becoming a master? I know the\u200b\u200b Ladder can have low Status masters, but if you get too good, are you kicked upstairs?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooooort of?<br /> <br /> Again*, you can't sit on the sidelines of an Order and expect to get Status, so if you're a low status member of an Order becasue you're off chasing your own Obsession butterflies and attain Mastery of an Arcanum, you're <i>probably</i> not going to gain esteem <i>as</i> a member of that order. On the other hand, if you're active and reliable <i>as</i> a member, then the attainment of mastery is likely to to more directly result in the rise of your esteem in the eyes of your peers.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, the game <i>mostly</i> assumes these two things are inter-related most of the time-one joins an Order to take advantage of the resources that makes it easier to expand your grasp of magic, the needs of the Order create opportunitiies for that expansion, fulfilling those needs raises your general appraisal with the order, your Obsessions become larger and grander the more powerful you get, that relative size turns into benefits and opportunities for others in the Order, and so on.<br /> <br /> But because they aren't synonymous with each other, the game has to understand how the two are viewed and feared and/or respected by others on their own, and in that regards, mastery of the Arcana is a more universal signifier of action and knowledge than the more politcally biased nature of Status. When you take those two with that in mind and reintroduce them to each other, you get the rough disparity we started with- they probably rise together when you work the two together, but only gain esteem as a Master if you don't-which is not <i>nothing</i>.<br /> <br /> Some Orders are going to have some flex and stretch on that-the Silver Ladder, as noted, and the Mysterium are more likely to lean towards giving Status with Mastery, the Arrow and the Guardians are less likely, and the Free Council is a general mess on the subject given how the democratic nature of the Sect makes status even more wibbly due to the fluid inter-relation between popularity and mastery of the Arcana can and can't be-But as a general rule, if you're active, it will, if you're not, it won't.<br /> <br /> *Barring, again, exceptional circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-09-2023, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T12:51:49-08:00","id":1502629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502621#post1502621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question: Do you automatically get rank when becoming a master? I know the\u200b\u200b Ladder can have low Status masters, but if you get too good, are you kicked upstairs?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a little unclear. As far as 1e went, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> covers it well.<br /> <br /> The big problem is page 71-2 in the 2e core. Apparently if you're a master, you &quot;have the right to be a magister&quot;... I'm not sure how that's supposed to look in practice, and I'm not sure if we're supposed to take from that there are now two different kinds of magister? More broadly, how much of the Convocation described in Silver Ladder carries over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T13:22:45-08:00","id":1502633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502629#post1502629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a little unclear. As far as 1e went, I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> covers it well.<br /> <br /> The big problem is page 71-2 in the 2e core. Apparently if you're a master, you &quot;have the right to be a magister&quot;... I'm not sure how that's supposed to look in practice, and I'm not sure if we're supposed to take from that there are now two different kinds of magister? More broadly, how much of the Convocation described in Silver Ladder carries over?</div> </div> </div> </div>This a world with the Demon, Demon, Demon Problem, so two kinds of magisters are the norm.<br /> <br /> Convocations are.....well, they're not an exception to the usual rules, but it is an exceptional occasion.<br /> <br /> Anyways, in theory, the principle is that any Master can basically claim a right to take on the responsibility and activity of arranging, directing, and maintaining a Convocation, a task that is theoretically always welcome because Convocations are big, hard to arrange things that can always do with the power and resources of anyone whose put in the work to become a Master.<br /> <br /> In <i>practice</i>, this can potentially be a political clusterfuck given the purpose of the convocation and the feelings of the masters involved. As a minor example, let's say the Arrow Caucuses of the American West have put up a call for a Convocation for getting a top down perspective on the last season or two's activities from enemies and generally coordinating what the forward action's going to be between them. As a rule, you want the Adamant Sages and Thunderbolt Guardians there-you probably do not want Johnny Teethkicker, a Talon in the arrow because he's too busy kicking in teeth for his own obscure purposes, to be part of the planning and scheduling, because he's pretty demonstrably always distracted by his practice of just randomly kicking in people's teeth. This can be a problem when he, as a Master because his Obsession with kicking teeth in has yielded results for him personally, exercises his right to be a magister for the Convocation. You can imagine the actual leaders of the Arrow Caucuses doing their level best to convince him that he doesn't want to arrange a Convocation because he'd be happier kicking in teeth, but if he insists, he has to be permitted a role in planning and arranging the Convcation and specific roles in keeping it going when it happens, which means, strictly speaking, the Convocation is just gonna have to risk possibly falling down as he eventually and invariably pursues his Mystery of choice that is wrapped up in the inexplicable art of kicking in teeth. Or maybe it goes fine, but that doesn't stop the political kerfuffle at the start.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in the post that I'm waiting to be re-allowed, there is a general understanding that for mages in the orders, Status and Mastery are very likely to inter-related to each other as a rule. The role of Magister and it's strict relationship to Mastery for Convocation usually relies on this, but allows narrative wrinkles and pecularities for Order and Sect-centered scenarios, but at the same time also allows for Convocations within Pentacle territories that account for and accomodate solitaires, cabals, Legacies and Nameless Orders outside of the system without much Order-based fuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T13:53:03-08:00","id":1502638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502633#post1502633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This a world with the Demon, Demon, Demon Problem, so two kinds of magisters are the norm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are at least not likely to arise in the same conversation; this is the Pentacle having one title for two different roles; plus, magisters as a title for high ranking Order members aren't mentioned in the 2e core. Like, I'm not saying it's wrong (actually, I think mages grumbling about who's a 'true' magister or not could be fun); just that if Tome of the Pentacle turns up one day, and the Neophyte/Famulus/Magister arrangement is just gone, I wouldn't be massively surprised.<br /> <br /> Same for your example. It's logical, and would run well, but I'm not certain that that's what the text is trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T14:38:09-08:00","id":1502643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1502114-what-do-i-have-to-do-to-keep-my-high-consilium-order-status?p=1502638#post1502638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are at least not likely to arise in the same conversation; this is the Pentacle having one title for two different roles; plus, magisters as a title for high ranking Order members aren't mentioned in the 2e core. Like, I'm not saying it's wrong (actually, I think mages grumbling about who's a 'true' magister or not could be fun); just that if Tome of the Pentacle turns up one day, and the Neophyte/Famulus/Magister arrangement is just gone, I wouldn't be massively surprised.<br /> <br /> Same for your example. It's logical, and would run well, but I'm not certain that that's what the text is trying to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2nd has the title of Emissary as a distinct role in two Orders. The Repeating Nomenclature Problem may colloquially be known as the Demon, Demon, or Demon Problem, but it has <i>many</i> forms. Anyways, the order books are not my main area of verse for Mage, I can't speak for too much of the organizational nuances brought up in those.<br /> <br /> The thing about Magisters being high ranking Order members doesn't explicitly have to be text for it to form something of a norm. The Sects and the Orders(/Ministries) thereof are massively potent resources for Mages seeking to master the Arcana, and engagement with the needs and wants of them are likewise potent opportunites for the same. I mentioned in the last post* that Status and Mastery are often inter-related because doing the things that raises one's esteem in an Order and likely awards authority to that esteem and the things that expand a mage's identity and ability to grasp magic are often intertwined enough to create the illusion of being the same. It's easier to become a Master by joining an Order and doing Order things than working outside of them, and it's easier to gain Status in an Order by doing Order things.<br /> <br /> That said, they aren't the same thing this-this is neither the changeling Courts nor the Arisen Guilds-and the thing about Magister being a position of authority that is demarcated strictly and solely by Mastery of the Arcana is that it keeps the overall settings central conceit of the universal metric of esteem <i>being</i> that Mastery of the Arcana squarely where it is.<br /> <br /> A Magister doesn't need be a rank 4/5 Order member, but rank 4/5 Order members are more likely to be Magisters than non-rank 4/5 Order members, because the Orders make the pursuit of Mastery easier the more you invest in them.<br /> <br /> *and the post before that, when it gets approved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T18:28:46-08:00","id":1503416,"title":"","content":"I found that the Order books tended to be consistent with the idea that the term &quot;magister&quot; tended to be applied to powerful mages who were immersed in the deeper esoterics of their Order's philosophy and mysticism, and the Silver Ladder book extended that concept with the point of &quot;these people are assumed to have a sense of communion with the Oracles that makes them qualified to run a Convocation&quot;. It appeared to be a distinction from what the books described as the actual hierarchical ranks of a caucus that Status could be a prerequisite for/equivalent to, even if at times the concept overlapped (most apparent with the Hierophants of the Mysterium).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it was one of those details that a Second Edition would come at as constituting an unnecessary and confusing extra layer of complexity that should be pared down. For the moment I think it suffices to say that Magister is a term for a mage (regardless of Order) whose mastery makes them eligible to be part of the managing body of a Convocation, that the top ranks of the Orders such as Deacon or Epopt absorb some of the qualities ascribed to magisters before, and that somebody most focused on more esoteric parts of the Mysteries can exist regardless of Status or Arcanum level.<br /> <br /> I feel as though maintaining Status ought to be viewed as a nuanced thing that acknowledges some common foibles of human character and institutions; that once a person attains high rank it can be hard to shift them even if their dedication seems to waver simply through a sense of inertia in the lower ranks, a lacking sense of procedure of and right to do so along with lingering good will from the process that led to their rise in the first place. I think the circumstances of the Diamond Orders have a tendency to select for people who demonstrate their dedication as they rise up the ranks, that it's unlikely to get somebody who can become a Deacon or Adamant Sage without internalizing the motives for those offices along the way, but in cases where they are idle or perhaps their assumption of the title was a bad call in the first place a lot of people can stall in uncertainty about doing anything in response to it.<br /> <br /> I think some of this would consider the extent to which Orders aren't exactly centralised organisations with a core body that makes the promotion decisions and holds those within them to account. I'd say that in most cases your caucus's Deacon was chosen for the role by a preceding Deacon. That simplifies some angles on it and complicates others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}